          "Type": "Terraform Plan JSON Security Check",
          "ID": "AZU-0058",
          "Title": "Storage account should use geo-redundant replication",
          "Description": "Geo-redundant storage (GRS) replicates your data to a secondary region that is hundreds of miles away from the primary region.\nThis provides an additional level of durability for your data in the event of a complete regional outage or a disaster.\nOptions include GRS, RAGRS, GZRS, and RAGZRS for geo-redundancy.\n",
          "Message": "Storage account does not use geo-redundant replication.",
          "Namespace": "builtin.azure.storage.azure0058",
          "Query": "data.builtin.azure.storage.azure0058.deny",
          "Resolution": "Configure storage account to use geo-redundant replication (GRS, RAGRS, GZRS, or RAGZRS)",
